## 9. Writing-style rules

- **No em-dashes (—) anywhere** in the manuscript. Use commas, parentheses, colons, or sentence splits. Keep hyphens in compound terms (Bound-and-Gap, five-phase, model-agnostic, AMR-elevator) and `--` page ranges in BibTeX.
- **Chinese version of any bilingual passage:** plain words, **no math symbols** (Φ → "三维表示"; H_up → "结构性天花板"; M_Φ → "可回收余量"; GAP → "差距/价值"). Keep proper method names (Bound-and-Gap, Model-Dominance Hedge Rule, Wasserstein, Smart-Predict-then-Optimize).
- Citation years: use the **formal journal year**, not the arXiv year (Elmachtoub & Grigas **2022**, not 2020; Vera et al. **2021**, not 2020).

